{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_016yuVWRX8ThaKiG4XCguv7s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-user personal productivity + R&D mission-control system, built for J.C. Liechty and running locally on the `PUTER`/`gwl-server` desktop. Grounded claims:\n\n- **Purpose â€” a personal GTD-style task system.** It tracks tasks, projects, and captured ideas across life domains (academic, commercial, family, writing) as plain markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`), with a full task lifecycle (active â†’ done â†’ cancelled / saved-for-later â†’ restored). Markdown is the single source of truth â€” no database, no binary formats.\n\n- **What it ships as a running app â€” `anchor_gui.py`.** A self-contained, stdlib-only Python HTTP server bound to `http://localhost:8777`, owned by the NSSM Windows service `anchor` (auto-start, persistent). It regenerates the dashboard HTML on every request and writes changes back to markdown directly via a REST-ish `/api/*` surface. `anchor.py` is a CLI mirror of the same logic that also emits a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Its larger ambition â€” a \"Mission Control / Project Cockpit\" for trio-driven R&D.** Each project gets a window where three lanes â€” **Research â†’ Planning â†’ Build** (mapped to the skills researchPrime Â· Crucible Â· Foreman) â€” run as **durable, isolated, server-side terminal sessions**. The locked North Star: each lane is a tile with one honest status light (green=working, amber=needs-you, red=crashed, grey=idle/done); clicking expands an inline panel (summary on top, a real resizable xterm.js terminal below) rather than navigating away; a new session loads its lane skill **once**, greets once, then behaves like a normal Claude/Gemini session.\n\n- **The technical substrate it ships (v2â†’v4, all built & merged to master).** Real **ConPTY terminals** via the one declared native exception `pywinpty` (lazy, `pty_manager.py` only); **per-session git-worktree isolation**; a durable session registry under `.anchor/`; **cached, adversarially-grounded session + project summaries** (generate-twice + grounding filter through a stubbable runner seam); a stage-handoff mechanism; ephemeral deliverable **previews** on OS-assigned ports hard-guarded `â‰  8777`; an **engine toggle** (Claudeâ†”Gemini, Gemini research-only); and Ghost World Labs branding (\"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\").\n\n- **It self-tests.** `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs daily at 5 AM via Task Scheduler, parsing every markdown file, exercising every endpoint, and walking the full v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces **fully stubbed** (no live `claude`, never touching the live `:8777` service or real data), writing `health_reports/YYYY-MM-DD.md`.\n\n- **Constraints that define it.** Single folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`), no OneDrive/syncing, local Git; **Python stdlib only** with the single `pywinpty` terminal exception, enforced by `distro.py`'s import scan; everything must stay plain-text and accessible from any CLI tool.\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: the declared deliverable is just `anchor_gui.py`, but in practice the project ships a sizable module ecosystem around it (`rnd_registry.py`, `sessions.py`, `summarizer.py`, `pty_manager.py`, `terminal_session.py`, `deliverables.py`, etc.) â€” the \"deliverable\" pin is narrower than the actual shipped surface."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24728,"cache_read_input_tokens":20597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24728},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"61d7e1ca-1067-4df4-adc9-76592e7dddba","uuid":"49247e43-5410-4500-a780-2b826cc93f34","request_id":"req_011Cc1Yv1v7WzASmaFa8TcRP"}
